// Dead Air: Refined - guided GTAO filter, 8x8 box (filter pass).
//
// Ported from IX-Ray (gamedata\shaders\d3d11\gtao_filter.ps.hlsl, author LVutner;
// local linear model / guided filter after Bart Wronski). One structural change:
// the donor reads a packed R32_UINT target with a single GatherRed and unpacks
// (view-z, AO) by bit tricks; our target is R16G16_FLOAT (x = view-z, y = AO),
// so each fetch is GatherRed for the guide plus GatherGreen for the signal -
// same values (both were 16-bit halves in the donor too), twice the gathers,
// still far cheaper than 64 point taps. The offsets stay spelled out because
// Gather offsets must be immediate literals.
//
// The 8x8 window is anchored half a texel up-left of the pixel (the donor notes
// the same shift); like the donor's combine, ours samples the result at plain
// texcoords - the half-texel skew is invisible after the linear-model fit.
//
// Reads $user$gtao_0, writes the final AO into $user$ssao_temp (R16F), which
// combine_1 samples as s_occ. Full resolution. The body is gtao_filter_pixel (gtao.h),
// shared with gtao_filter.cs.

#include "gtao.h"

// The full input signature stays: the pass links against da_fullscreen.vs.
float main(float2 tc0 : TEXCOORD0, float4 hpos : SV_Position) : SV_Target
{
    DA_STAGE_EXACT float r = gtao_filter_pixel(uint2(hpos.xy));
    return r;
}
